ay allow them to bluff on river — but also lets you see river cheaply.\n\nBut you want to **build the pot when you\'re getting good equity** — semi-bluffing now gains value.\n\nGiven stack sizes (you have 19,900), betting 100 is small (0.5% of stack), low risk.\n\nAlso, you are behind in total chips (-10,812 cumulative), so need to gain back.\n\nThus, a small **bet of 100** (minimum) is a solid semi-bluff:  \n- Denies equity to opponents  \n- May win immediately  \n- If called, you still have ~18% to win\n\nChecking risks letting opponent check back and see free river — reducing your chances to win without improvement.\n\nTherefore, better to **bet 100**\n\nReason:  \nI have a strong draw (9 outs to flush) and minimal showdown value. Given opponent has checked twice, they likely have a weak or marginal hand. A small bet of 100 acts as a semi-bluff, applying pressure and potentially winning the pot immediately while also building the pot for when I hit my flush on the river.\n\nAnswer: 100'}
